content-type:  text/html

Console:
SyntaxError: Unexpected token ''<'', "<!DOCTYPE "... is not valid JSON

Statement: "A response came back from the server side; the SyntaxError comes from parsing an HTML error page as JSON, not from a network failure."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. A status code and response headers can only exist if an HTTP response arrived, so the network worked. The 502 page was produced by the gateway in front of the API, its Content-Type is text/html, and res.json() threw while parsing the leading ''<''. The common mistake is to treat every exception around fetch() as "offline"; a network failure would show (failed) in the Status column and no status code at all.', 1, 5
