Browser console: TimeoutError: signal timed out (after 3.0 s)

API access log for the same request:
10:02:11.904 POST /submissions 201 4180ms

Statement: "The submission was saved even though the client saw a timeout, so retrying this POST automatically, without an idempotency key, can create a duplicate submission."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. A client timeout only stops the client from waiting; it does not cancel work the server already started. The access log shows the server answered 201 Created after 4.18 s, so the submission exists. POST is not idempotent (RFC 9110, section 9.2.2), so sending it again creates a second submission. Retry a POST only when the server can recognise the repeat, for example with an Idempotency-Key header that the client reuses for every attempt of the same action. The misconception is that a timeout means "nothing happened": it means "I do not know what happened".', 2, 5
