Statement: "For this response, the catch block runs and sets courses to an empty array."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. fetch() resolves for every HTTP response, including 4xx and 5xx; it rejects only when no response arrives (network error, CORS block, abort). The 503 body is valid JSON, so res.json() returns the object {"error":"service_unavailable"}. That object has no length property, courses.length is undefined, which is falsy, and the page shows "You have no courses yet" without ever entering the catch block. The misconception is that fetch throws on HTTP errors; you have to check res.ok or res.status yourself before you treat the body as data.', 1, 5
