Statement: "The list can end up showing the results for \"p\" while the search box shows \"py\"."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. Both requests are in flight at the same time and responses do not arrive in the order the requests were sent. The "py" response arrives after about 180 ms and is rendered; the "p" response arrives later and overwrites it, so the newest input shows the oldest answer. The fix is to cancel the previous request with an AbortController (and ignore the AbortError it causes), or to remember which request is the latest and drop any other response. The misconception is that a later request always finishes later.', 2, 5
